Below is an outline of what’s happening, why it’s wrong, and the minimal patch to fix it.

1. Bug description & root cause  
   – In `StyledRadioButtonBox`, the background‐color is always pulled from `theme.radioButton.check.background.color` unconditionally, so every radio “box” is painted, even when it isn’t checked.  
   – The component never looks at `props.checked`, so it has no way to know “only paint when checked.”  

2. Fix  
   – Make the styled component only set `background-color` when it receives `props.checked`.  
   – Pass the `checked` prop down from the `<RadioButton>` so that `StyledRadioButtonBox` can see it.

3. Patches  
   – In `src/js/components/RadioButton/StyledRadioButton.js`, wrap background styling in a `props.checked` guard.  
   – In `src/js/components/RadioButton/RadioButton.js`, pass `checked={checked}` into `<StyledRadioButtonBox />`.

